const faqs = [
  { q: "Is Brampton water hard?", a: "Yes. Brampton gets treated Lake Ontario water through the Region of Peel South Peel system. It is in the hard range, roughly 7 to 10 grains per gallon, which is enough to cause scale on fixtures, spots on dishes and buildup in water heaters. Peel Region publishes yearly water quality reports if you want the exact numbers." },
  { q: "How much does a water softener cost in Brampton?", a: "It depends on your water hardness, household size, the system you choose and how much plumbing work the location needs. Contact us for a price. We test your water for free and give you a clear quote before any work starts." },
  { q: "Do you offer a free water test?", a: "Yes. We test hardness at your tap for free, and check for iron on well water, so the softener is sized properly." },
  { q: "How long does a water softener installation take?", a: "Most city water softener installations in a basement or utility room take about half a day. Well water systems with extra filters can take longer." },
  { q: "Will a water softener make my water salty?", a: "No, softened water does not taste salty. A small amount of sodium is added during softening, which goes up with your water hardness. If you are on a low-sodium diet, many homes keep a hard water tap for drinking, add a reverse osmosis system at the kitchen sink, or use potassium chloride instead of salt." },
  { q: "Do I need a softener and an RO system?", a: "They do different jobs. A softener protects the whole house from scale. An RO system filters drinking water at the kitchen sink. Many families use both, which is why we offer a Softener + RO combo." },
  { q: "Can you install a softener for well water in Caledon?", a: "Yes. Well water often has higher hardness and can carry iron or sulphur. We test the water first and may add an iron or sulphur filter, sediment prefilter or UV before the softener." },
  { q: "How often do I add salt?", a: "Most homes add a bag or two of softener salt every few weeks to a couple of months, depending on water use and hardness. We set the system up efficiently and show you what to check." },
  { q: "Can you replace or fix my old water softener?", a: "Yes. We can repair, re-pipe, or replace an older softener, including the bypass, drain and connections, and remove the old unit." },
  { q: "Does a softener help my water heater?", a: "Yes. Soft water reduces the scale that builds up inside tank and tankless water heaters, which helps them run more efficiently and can reduce descaling and repairs." },
  { q: "Is a salt-free water conditioner the same as a softener?", a: "No. A salt-free conditioner does not remove hardness minerals; it changes them so they are less likely to stick as scale. It can suit condos without a drain, but a salt-based softener is the stronger choice for most Brampton homes." },
];

const areas = [
  { name: "Brampton", href: "brampton-plumber.html" },
