---

<BaseLayout title={title} description={description} canonical={canonical} schemas={schemas}>
  <SiteHeader />

  <main class="ws">
    <!-- HERO -->
    <section class="ws-hero">
      <div class="ws-hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">Water softener · Brampton &amp; GTA</p>
        <h1>Water Softener Brampton</h1>
        <p class="ws-lead">
          Hard water is leaving scale on your taps, spots on your dishes and buildup in your water heater.
          Fateh Plumbing &amp; Electric installs water softeners in Brampton for city water and well water, starting
          with a <strong>free water hardness test</strong> so your system is sized right the first time.
        </p>
        <div class="ws-actions">
          <a class="button" href="book-online.html">Book free water test</a>
          <a class="button secondary" href="tel:+16479809211">Call 647-980-9211</a>
        </div>
        <ul class="ws-proof">
          <li>Licensed &amp; insured plumbers</li>
          <li>City &amp; well water systems</li>
          <li>Clean, code-aware installs</li>
        </ul>
      </div>
      <figure class="ws-hero-art ws-hero-img">
        <img src="/assets/service-photos/water-softener-installation-brampton.webp" alt="Water softener system with mineral tank, digital control valve and brine tank" width="1000" height="1000" loading="eager" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async">
      </figure>
    </section>

    <!-- TRUST STRIP -->
    <section class="ws-trust" aria-label="Why homeowners choose Fateh">
      <div><strong>Free</strong><span>on-site water hardness test</span></div>
      <div><strong>Licensed</strong><span>plumbers, WSIB covered</span></div>
      <div><strong>$5M</strong><span>liability insurance</span></div>
      <div><strong>10+ years</strong><span>serving Brampton &amp; the GTA</span></div>
    </section>

    <!-- QUICK ANSWER -->
    <section class="ws-wrap ws-answer">
      <h2>What does a water softener do?</h2>
      <p>
        A water softener removes the calcium and magnesium that make water "hard." Water passes through a tank of resin beads
        that trap the hardness minerals and swap them for a small amount of sodium (or potassium). The result is soft water
        throughout the house: less scale on fixtures, no spots on dishes, better lather, and less buildup inside your water heater,
        dishwasher and washing machine.
      </p>
    </section>

    <!-- SIGNS -->
    <section class="ws-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Hard water signs</p>
      <h2>Do you have hard water? Look for these signs</h2>
      <div class="ws-signs">
        {signs.map((s) => (
          <article>
            <span class={`ws-ico ws-ico-${s.icon}`} aria-hidden="true"></span>
            <h3>{s.title}</h3>
            <p>{s.text}</p>
          </article>
        ))}
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- BRAMPTON WATER -->
    <section class="ws-band">
      <div class="ws-wrap ws-local">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Brampton water hardness</p>
          <h2>Why water softeners are common in Brampton homes</h2>
          <p>
            Brampton, Mississauga and south Caledon (including Bolton) get treated Lake Ontario water through the Region of Peel's
            South Peel drinking water system. The water is safe to drink, but it is naturally <strong>hard</strong>: roughly
            7 to 10 grains per gallon. That is enough to leave scale on fixtures, spots on glass and buildup inside water heaters
            and appliances over time.
          </p>
          <p>
            Many homes in north Caledon and rural areas are on private wells or smaller groundwater systems. Well water is often
            harder than lake water and can also carry iron (orange or brown stains) or sulphur (a rotten egg smell), so it needs
            testing before choosing a system.
          </p>
          <p class="ws-source">
            Check your area's numbers in the <a href="https://www.peelregion.ca/water/drinking-water/water-quality/water-quality-reports" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Region of Peel water quality reports</a>,
            and learn more about water hardness from <a href="https://www.canada.ca/en/health-canada/services/environmental-workplace-health/water-quality/drinking-water.html" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Health Canada</a>.
          </p>
        </div>
        <div class="ws-table-card">
          <table>
            <caption>Typical water by area</caption>
            <thead><tr><th>Area</th><th>Water source</th><th>What to expect</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              <tr><td>Brampton</td><td>Lake Ontario (South Peel)</td><td>Hard, about 7–10 gpg</td></tr>
              <tr><td>Mississauga</td><td>Lake Ontario (South Peel)</td><td>Hard, about 7–10 gpg</td></tr>
              <tr><td>South Caledon / Bolton</td><td>Lake Ontario (South Peel)</td><td>Hard, about 7–10 gpg</td></tr>
              <tr><td>North Caledon &amp; rural</td><td>Wells / groundwater</td><td>Often harder, may have iron</td></tr>
            </tbody>
          </table>
          <p class="ws-small">gpg = grains per gallon. Every home is different; your free water test gives the real number.</p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- CITY vs WELL -->
    <section class="ws-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Choose your water type</p>
      <h2>City water or well water?</h2>
      <div class="ws-two">
        <article class="ws-type">
          <h3>City water</h3>
          <p>Treated municipal water from Lake Ontario. The main problem is hardness, so a properly sized softener is usually all you need.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Hardness: moderate to hard</li>
            <li>Iron and sulphur: not usually a concern</li>
            <li>Best fit: City Water Softener, or Softener + RO</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="ws-link" href="#city">See City Water Softener</a>
        </article>
        <article class="ws-type">
          <h3>Well water</h3>
          <p>Private well water can be very hard and may include iron, sulphur or sediment. The system is built in stages after a water test.</p>
          <ul>
            <li>Hardness: often higher than city water</li>
            <li>Iron, manganese, sulphur and sediment: possible</li>
            <li>Best fit: Well Water System (filter + softener)</li>
          </ul>
          <a class="ws-link" href="#well">See Well Water System</a>
        </article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- PACKAGES -->
    <section class="ws-band">
      <div class="ws-wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">Water softener packages</p>
        <h2>Pick the package that fits your home</h2>
        <p class="ws-sub">Every package starts with a free water test. Pricing depends on your water, household size and installation space, so we quote after we see it.</p>
        <div class="ws-packages">
          {packages.map((p) => (
            <article id={p.id} class={p.featured ? "ws-pkg is-featured" : "ws-pkg"}>
              <span class="ws-tag">{p.tag}</span>
              <div class={p.art === "city" ? "ws-pkg-art ws-pkg-tall has-photo" : "ws-pkg-art ws-pkg-tall"} aria-hidden={p.art === "city" ? undefined : "true"}>
                {p.art === "city" && (
                  <img src="/assets/service-photos/city-water-softener-brampton.webp" alt="City water softener with mineral tank and brine tank installed on copper water lines in a basement" width="960" height="600" loading="lazy" decoding="async">
                )}
                {p.art === "well" && (
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 160 110"><rect x="14" y="30" width="28" height="72" rx="12" fill="#c2410c"/><rect x="12" y="20" width="32" height="14" rx="5" fill="#0f172a"/><rect x="58" y="18" width="32" height="84" rx="14" fill="#2f80e8"/><rect x="56" y="8" width="36" height="16" rx="5" fill="#0f172a"/><rect x="104" y="52" width="40" height="50" rx="6" fill="#e2e8f0" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/><path d="M42 40 H58 M90 60 C 98 60 98 56 104 56" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="3" fill="none"/></svg>
                )}
                {p.art === "combo" && (
                  <svg viewBox="0 0 160 110"><rect x="18" y="18" width="32" height="84" rx="14" fill="#2f80e8"/><rect x="16" y="8" width="36" height="16" rx="5" fill="#0f172a"/><rect x="74" y="64" width="72" height="38" rx="5" fill="#e2e8f0" stroke="#94a3b8" stroke-width="2"/><rect x="82" y="72" width="10" height="26" rx="4" fill="#38bdf8"/><rect x="98" y="72" width="10" height="26" rx="4" fill="#38bdf8"/><rect x="114" y="72" width="10" height="26" rx="4" fill="#38bdf8"/><path d="M128 64 V36 H112 V42" stroke="#64748b" stroke-width="4" fill="none" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="112" cy="48" r="3" fill="#38bdf8"/></svg>
                )}
              </div>
              <h3>{p.title}</h3>
              <p class="ws-best"><strong>Best for:</strong> {p.best}</p>
              <ul>{p.includes.map((i) => <li>{i}</li>)}</ul>
              <p class="ws-price">Price: <strong>Contact us for price</strong></p>
              <a class="button" href="book-online.html">Book free water test</a>
              {p.link && <a class="ws-link" href={p.link.href}>{p.link.text}</a>}
            </article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- HOW IT WORKS -->
    <section class="ws-wrap ws-how">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">How it works</p>
        <h2>How a water softener works</h2>
        <ol class="ws-numbered">
          <li><strong>Hard water enters the tank.</strong> Water flows through a bed of resin beads inside the mineral tank.</li>
          <li><strong>Minerals are swapped out.</strong> The beads grab calcium and magnesium and release a small amount of sodium or potassium.</li>
          <li><strong>Soft water goes to the house.</strong> Every tap, shower and appliance gets softened water.</li>
          <li><strong>The system cleans itself.</strong> When the beads are full, the softener rinses them with salty brine from the brine tank and sends the hardness down the drain. Modern units do this based on how much water you actually use.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <aside class="ws-note">
        <h3>Why a licensed plumber matters</h3>
        <ul>
          <li>The drain line needs an <strong>air gap</strong> so wastewater can never back up into your water system.</li>
          <li>A <strong>bypass valve</strong> lets you shut the softener off without shutting off the house.</li>
          <li>Outdoor taps and the kitchen drinking line can be left on hard water if you want.</li>
          <li>Connections are pressure-tested so there are no slow leaks behind the unit.</li>
        </ul>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <!-- PROCESS -->
    <section class="ws-band">
      <div class="ws-wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">Our installation process</p>
        <h2>From free water test to soft water in four steps</h2>
        <div class="ws-steps">
          {steps.map((s, i) => (
            <article><span>{i + 1}</span><h3>{s.title}</h3><p>{s.text}</p></article>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SIZING -->
    <section class="ws-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Sizing guide</p>
      <h2>What size water softener do I need?</h2>
      <p class="ws-sub">Softeners are rated in "grains" — how much hardness they can remove before cleaning themselves. This is a rough guide for Brampton city water; your water test decides the final size.</p>
      <div class="ws-table-card">
        <table>
          <thead><tr><th>Household</th><th>Typical softener size</th><th>Common for</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {sizing.map((r) => <tr><td>{r.people}</td><td>{r.capacity}</td><td>{r.note}</td></tr>)}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- COMPARE -->
    <section class="ws-band">
      <div class="ws-wrap">
        <p class="eyebrow">Compare options</p>
        <h2>Water softener vs salt-free conditioner vs reverse osmosis</h2>
        <div class="ws-table-card ws-scroll">
          <table>
            <thead><tr><th></th><th>Water softener</th><th>Salt-free conditioner</th><th>Reverse osmosis</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
              {compareRows.map((r) => <tr><td>{r.label}</td><td>{r.softener}</td><td>{r.salt}</td><td>{r.ro}</td></tr>)}
            </tbody>
          </table>
        </div>
        <p class="ws-sub">Not sure? Most Brampton homes start with a softener. Add an <a href="reverse-osmosis-system.html">RO drinking water system</a> if taste is the main concern.</p>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- WHY FATEH -->
    <section class="ws-wrap">
      <p class="eyebrow">Why Fateh</p>
      <h2>Why Brampton homeowners call Fateh for water softeners</h2>
      <div class="ws-why">
        <article><h3>Plumbers, not just a sales visit</h3><p>Licensed plumbers do the install, so drains, bypasses and connections are done properly the first time.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Free water test, honest sizing</h3><p>We size the system to your water and household, not the biggest unit on the truck.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Any brand, new or existing</h3><p>New installs, replacements, re-piping and repairs on existing softeners.</p></article>
        <article><h3>Plumbing + electrical in one call</h3><p>If the location needs an outlet or other work, one team can handle it.</p></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- SERVICE AREA -->
    <section class="ws-band">
      <div class="ws-wrap ws-area">
        <div>
          <p class="eyebrow">Service area</p>
          <h2>Water softener installation in Brampton and nearby GTA cities</h2>
          <p>We install and service water softeners across Brampton, including {neighbourhoods.join(", ")}, and nearby cities:</p>
          <ul class="ws-chips">
            {areas.map((a) => <li><a href={a.href}>{a.name}</a></li>)}
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div class="ws-related">
          <h3>Related water services</h3>
          {related.map((r) => (
            <a href={r.href}><strong>{r.title}</strong><span>{r.text}</span></a>
          ))}
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- FAQ -->
    <section class="ws-wrap ws-faq">
      <p class="eyebrow">Water softener FAQ</p>
      <h2>Water softener questions from Brampton homeowners</h2>
      {faqs.map((f) => (
        <details>
          <summary>{f.q}</summary>
          <p>{f.a}</p>
        </details>
